[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4187341134","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/118188#issuecomment-4187341134","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118188","id":4187341134,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc75lcFO","user":{"login":"mrjustaguy","id":50302479,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwMzAyNDc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/50302479?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy","html_url":"https://github.com/mrjustaguy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-04T16:15:30Z","updated_at":"2026-04-04T16:15:30Z","body":"This is an expected behavior of MSAA, the Depth Buffer is resolved and the Post effects are dealing with Depth Values that aren't accurately representing the actual depths of all the samples, and rather only handle one depth sample per pixel.\n\nThis effect also happens with other Post Processing effects like Proximity Fade, SSAO etc, but not ones that purely happen with Color like Glow.\n\nI do not believe there is much that can be done regarding this issue without a lot of added complexity and/or massive performance penalties, and IIRC this also happens with Per Sample Rate Shading (for which there is a long stale PR)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4187341134/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4187393231","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/118188#issuecomment-4187393231","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118188","id":4187393231,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc75lozP","user":{"login":"20k","id":755197,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc1NTE5Nw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/755197?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/20k","html_url":"https://github.com/20k","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/20k/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/20k/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/20k/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/20k/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/20k/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/20k/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/20k/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/20k/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/20k/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-04T16:47:46Z","updated_at":"2026-04-04T16:47:46Z","body":"Interesting, I wonder if it'd be worth adding a warning when enabling effects that trigger a resolve, or noting in the docs what effects are unusable with MSAA - as it took me a number of days to track this down\n\nIs there anything that would especially block an MSAA aware subsurface scattering implementation? My understanding is that this would largely involve opting SSS out of performing a resolve, and then making the SSS implementation MSAA aware which seems doable. There'd b